e Red Death, drenched in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask, appears and walks deliberately through all seven rooms. Enraged, Prince Prospero pursues the figure with a dagger, but when he confronts it in the black chamber, he collapses dead; the courtiers rush in only to discover the mask and robes are empty, revealing the Red Death itself has infiltrated their sanctuary, and one by one, all revelers die as the clock stops and darkness claims the abbey.\"\n    34→    }\n    35→  ],\n    36→  \"characters\": [\n    37→    {\n    38→      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n    39→      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n    40→      \"aliases\": [\n    41→        \"the mummer\"\n    42→      ],\n    43→      \"role\": null,\n    44→      \"appearance\": null,\n    45→      \"personality\": null,\n    46→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    47→      \"descriptions\": [\n    48→        {\n    49→          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a bold and robust man who holds authority over a group of revellers in a secluded abbey. He reacts with intense anger and fear when confronted by a masked figure dressed as the Red Death, ultimately pursuing the intruder into a black chamber before being killed. His actions shift from commanding authority to panicked pursuit, ending in his death.\",\n    50→          \"source_position\": 10339,\n    51→          \"chapter_index\": null,\n    52→          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n    53→        }\n    54→      ],\n    55→      \"relationships\": {},\n    56→      \"evidence\": [\n    57→        {\n    58→          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero is described as bold and robust\",\n    59→          \"quote\": \"the prince was a bold and robust man\",\n    60→          \"position\": 11148,\n    61→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    62→        },\n    63→        {\n    64→          \"statement\": \"He commands the revellers and expresses outrage at the intruder\",\n    65→          \"quote\": \"insult us with this blasphemous mockery? Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n    66→          \"position\": 11148,\n    67→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    68→        },\n    69→        {\n    70→          \"statement\": \"He pursues the masked figure through multiple chambers\",\n    71→          \"quote\": \"the Prince Prospero, maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice, rushed hurriedly through the six chambers\",\n    72→          \"position\": 12389,\n    73→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    74→        },\n    75→        {\n    76→          \"statement\": \"He confronts the intruder in the black chamber and is killed\",\n    77→          \"quote\": \"turned suddenly and confronted his pursuer. There was a sharp cry -- and the dagger dropped gleaming upon the sable carpet, upon which, instantly afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\",\n    78→          \"position\": 12980,\n    79→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    80→        },\n    81→        {\n    82→          \"statement\": \"He is killed by the masked figure in the black chamber\",\n    83→          \"quote\": \"fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\",\n    84→          \"position\": 13136,\n    85→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    86→        }\n    87→      ],\n    88→      \"voice_notes\": null,\n    89→      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n    90→      \"mention_count\": 6,\n    91→      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    92→      \"is_narrator\": false,\n    93→      \"narrative_role\": null\n    94→    }\n    95→  ],\n    96→  \"pronunciations\": [\n    97→    {\n    98→      \"word\": \"Prospero\",\n    99→      \"flag_reason\": \"proper_noun\",\n   100→      \"occurrences\": 18,\n   101→      \"first_position\": 631,\n   102→      \"chapter_indices\": [\n   103→        1\n   104→      ],\n   105→      \"context_examples\": [\n   106→        \"...izure, progress and termina