h chime a reminder of mortality’s inevitability. Then, a chilling figure appears—dressed as the Red Death itself, with a mask resembling a corpse and robes drenched in blood. This spectral intruder moves with eerie calm through all seven rooms, uninvited and unchallenged, a living embodiment of the plague they sought to flee. Prince Prospero, enraged by the violation of his sanctuary and the mockery of his defiance, pursues the figure with a dagger, driven by pride and fear. His pursuit leads him into the black chamber, where the clock’s final chime echoes as he collapses, dead—revealing the horrifying truth that the figure was not a guest, but the plague incarnate.\\n\\nThe revelers, now gripped by terror, rush into the black chamber only to find the mask and robes empty, confirming that the Red Death has infiltrated their sanctuary not as a visitor, but as an inescapable force. One by one, they fall, succumbing to the same fate as those outside the abbey. The clock stops, the firelight flickers out, and darkness consumes the abbey, marking the end of their illusion of safety. The story concludes with the complete annihilation of the court, underscoring the futility of attempting to escape death through wealth, power, or isolation. The final image is one of absolute stillness—a world where even the most elaborate defenses cannot withstand the inevitability of mortality.\",\n  1433→      \"themes\": [\n  1434→        \"identity\",\n  1435→        \"ambition\",\n  1436→        \"loss\"\n  1437→      ],\n  1438→      \"narrative_style\": \"first-person retrospective\"\n  1439→    },\n  1440→    \"model_usage\": {\n  1441→      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n  1442→        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n  1443→        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n  1444→      },\n  1445→      \"Character Extraction\": {\n  1446→        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n  1447→        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n  1448→      },\n  1449→      \"Chapter Summaries\": {\n  1450→ 